[Debug] ----- Vuln Cause Analysis -----
The potential vulnerability is related to a Command Injection vulnerability. This vulnerability arises because the code explicitly states its intention to execute an external command, `openssl genpkey`, where a part of the command string, `<key_length>`, is a placeholder that will likely be replaced by a variable. If this variable is derived from untrusted input and is directly interpolated into the command string without proper sanitization or escaping, an attacker could inject malicious shell commands. These injected commands would then be executed by the underlying operating system, potentially leading to unauthorized code execution, data exfiltration, or system compromise.

